A record store refines the router’s state with past outcomes. In an idealized version, tasks fall into J J cells that share a record; ACRouter’s embedding-keyed store [ 4 ] is a richer instance. Cells arrive independently with probabilities ν j > 0 
u_{j}>0 . At the start of a round, each cell is uninformed ( U U ) or holds an informative ( I I ) or erroneous ( W W ) record. After the round, each record expires with probability δ j \delta_{j} , and the arriving cell receives an informative write with probability ω j \omega_{j} or an erroneous one with probability ψ j \psi_{j} , replacing its record; write types are independent of the past. Put r j = ω j + ψ j > 0 r_{j}=\omega_{j}+\psi_{j}>0 and α j = ( 1 − δ j ) ​ ( 1 − ν j ​ r j ) < 1 \alpha_{j}=(1-\delta_{j})(1-
u_{j}r_{j})<1 . Let v j s v_{j}^{s} and c j s c_{j}^{s} be the router’s expected value and cost in cell j j and record state s ∈ { U , I , W } s\in\{U,I,W\} , including the record update. Records are measured against the uninformed router, which writes at the same cost but routes as if uninformed and has efficiency η U = ∑ j ν j ​ v j U / ∑ j ν j ​ c j U \eta_{U}=\sum_{j}
u_{j}v_{j}^{U}/\sum_{j}
u_{j}c_{j}^{U} , by the gains g j s = ( v j s − v j U ) − η U ​ ( c j s − c j U ) g_{j}^{s}=(v_{j}^{s}-v_{j}^{U})-\eta_{U}(c_{j}^{s}-c_{j}^{U}) .
